{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Bow shot",
  "description": "A longbow loosed beside your ear in a wood: 'thwp-fff', not a note. The fingers let go and the string snaps forward, a short dry thrum with its buzz on top. At once the limbs kick forward and stop, a dull crowded wooden knock in the stave. As the arrow leaves, the string reaches the end of its travel and slaps the bracer, a flat leathery smack that chokes the thrum. The arrow's breathy hiss, with fletching flutter, falls in pitch and fades as it flies off. The trees give back a soft, short scatter.",
